  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n7÷3\\times 15\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷3$ and the $\\times 15:$\n\n$$\n7\\times 15÷3\n$$\n\nExpressing the division as a fraction, we arrive at:\n\n$$\n7\\times \\frac{15}{3}\n$$\n\nWe now solve:\n\n$$\n7\\times {{\\frac{15}{3}}_{⏟}}_{5}=7\\times 5=35\n$$",
